      {
        "sha": "e8fd183dff8e67697b1cac61e82dc40fd0caee69",
        "node_id": "C_kwDOFbd6J9oAKGU4ZmQxODNkZmY4ZTY3Njk3YjFjYWM2MWU4MmRjNDBmZDBjYWVlNjk",
        "commit": {
          "author": {
            "name": "Martin Sattlecker",
            "email": "120572403+msat-huawei@users.noreply.github.com",
            "date": "2025-08-07T15:45:42Z"
          },
          "committer": {
            "name": "GitHub",
            "email": "noreply@github.com",
            "date": "2025-08-07T15:45:42Z"
          },
          "message": "Build DXC without hct on Windows and use the built dxil.dll (#290)\n\nThe install script for the dxc previously installed the `dxil.dll` from\nthe Windows SDK instead of using the one from the install directory.\nI found that the `dxil.dll` from the Windows SDK is no longer compatible\nwith the 2505.1 executables when testing\nhttps://github.com/o3de/o3de/pull/19171\nCopying `dxil.dll` from a locally built dxc did however fix this\nproblem.\n\nI'm not sure why we ever used the `dxil.dll` from the Windows SDK\ninstead of the built one. On Linux and Mac there is no Windows SDK so\nthey use the built one without problems.\n\nThis PR also changes the build step from the `hct` build script to using\nCMake directly. As far as I can see hct is only a wrapper around CMake\nanyway.\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Martin Sattlecker <martin.sattlecker@huawei.com>",
          "tree": {
            "sha": "b0338d0b39749b584f712c463117b126cc82323e",
            "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/o3de/3p-package-source/git/trees/b0338d0b39749b584f712c463117b126cc82323e"
          },
          "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/o3de/3p-package-source/git/commits/e8fd183dff8e67697b1cac61e82dc40fd0caee69",
          "comment_count": 0,
          "verification": {
            "verified": true,
            "reason": "valid",
            "signature": "-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJolMonCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAiCIQAK4H9j3VB/on4IBUmX+XH2km\n3Dm9KPkUNYhwLVd35KMcWG0UdekNrzeKf1BqSENYZYKFaOZPzxA6wdTBOIAgU4Nm\nG8SQ4iPu5VzAzRvET3KkhnRaoXUaJoguAUWm1Ku5B/DDIwOYBtEqTZvfR+Jg4Tg6\ncqdYBSC+pDhIk9Z0dj331DPhMh86WP6+RxSr/8mREbgMU9FQiejSTMWeoxf1hVaL\nnVvKRTjneGe+6mrvOJp5lWJmQfF2Zi0R0dZW4o8InuCtIgoWwGi+eqDLJhcs/Dz6\nNlBfg3a4kkGxihKOpz1ITAfMffsL2IPtMgWqZEe7ZIYBynDtoN/pKt2Eaf3BkRei\nZJQMFq8hc8uDRCzE0NkB8XYHE5BtKTGzm/PytriFVfspA7OpEYZiS0/A5jNa8W6K\noTeSMsCunnBXbAL2K8vK4vExstWxoI5jngyTm4eMC4MpTY+aBcqUBRA402pSEQb3\niS83fWVCPbyre7Gm0EYYhNfGXDH+9uZqReisSfm5VhOIFVXEGLhqseSjb5Mxx1up\nRIu0KfTQPW17p/qepbkpvc4bxtyE60zgNAZcagp0KpuvpiCbET3oR7BHKNx1VQyk\n6mh+HWIFUFlejQdu87Hd+sPlN8p4sYGaWmlHUCwwZ22Fxk0YqNITGXGyGGgQEPT9\npnbM0Htm9g/kXF+HU1tv\n=G/If\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n",
            "payload": "tree b0338d0b39749b584f712c463117b126cc82323e\nparent 2dfc112793035a1ebe44793b3c3f7d481388e2a5\nauthor Martin Sattlecker <120572403+msat-huawei@users.noreply.github.com> 1754581542 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1754581542 -0700\n\nBuild DXC without hct on Windows and use the built dxil.dll (#290)\n\nThe install script for the dxc previously installed the `dxil.dll` from\nthe Windows SDK instead of using the one from the install directory.\nI found that the `dxil.dll` from the Windows SDK is no longer compatible\nwith the 2505.1 executables when testing\nhttps://github.com/o3de/o3de/pull/19171\nCopying `dxil.dll` from a locally built dxc did however fix this\nproblem.\n\nI'm not sure why we ever used the `dxil.dll` from the Windows SDK\ninstead of the built one. On Linux and Mac there is no Windows SDK so\nthey use the built one without problems.\n\nThis PR also changes the build step from the `hct` build script to using\nCMake directly. As far as I can see hct is only a wrapper around CMake\nanyway.\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Martin Sattlecker <martin.sattlecker@huawei.com>",
